<title>JAPAN: Japan current account surplus down 35.6% in Sept.</title>
<headline>Japan current account surplus down 35.6% in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's current account, the broadest measure of trade in goods and services, dropped 35.6 percent from a year earlier to 727.40 billion yen in September, the Finance Ministry announced on Monday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the balance of payments figures follows:</p>
<p>(Unadjusted, in yen)     SEPT	  AUG	YEAR AGO</p>
<p>Current Acct Balance  +727.4 bln  +460.6 bln +1.129 trln</p>
<p> -Goods and Services  +352.2 bln   +22.9 bln  +879.5 bln</p>
<p>    Trade Balance     +973.7 bln  +566.7 bln +1.336 trln</p>
<p>	 Exports	  3.766 trln  3.374 trln  3.756 trln</p>
<p>	 Imports	  2.792 trln  2.808 trln  2.420 trln</p>
<p>    Services Balance  -621.5 bln  -543.8 bln  -456.7 bln</p>
<p> -Income Balance	+441.9 bln  +511.2 bln  +302.5 bln</p>
<p> -Current Transfers    -66.6 bln   -73.5 bln   -52.4 bln</p>
<p>(Adjusted, in yen)	 SEPT	     AUG</p>
<p>Current Account Balance+520.5 bln    +882.5 bln</p>
<p> -Goods and Services    +89.1 bln    +383.1 bln</p>
<p>    Trade Balance	+701.6 bln    +883.9 bln</p>
<p>	 Exports	  +3.496 trln   +3.638 trln</p>
<p>	 Imports	  +2.794 trln   +2.754 trln</p>
<p>    Services Balance   -612.6 bln    -500.7 bln</p>
<p> -Income Balance	 +478.9 bln    +538.6 bln</p>
<p> -Current Transfers     -47.5 bln     -39.3 bln</p>
<p>The following figures show the unadjusted balance in Japan's capital and financial accounts (in yen):</p>
<p>				 SEPT	  AUG	YEAR AGO</p>
<p>Capital/Financial Acct  -54.1 bln   +13.6 bln  -164.6 bln</p>
<p> -Financial Account     -31.6 bln   +40.3 bln  -137.7 bln</p>
<p>  Direct Investment    -138.6 bln  -196.1 bln   -74.8 bln</p>
<p>  Portfolio Investment-2.611 trln -1.082 trln  +103.8 bln</p>
<p>  Other Investmen   t +2.718 trln +1.318 trln  -166.7 bln</p>
<p> -Capital Account	 -22.5 bln   -26.7 bln   -26.9 bln</p>
